FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] src/runtime.rs:465 — `time.sleep` calls `Duration::from_secs_f64(seconds)` with no validation — `time.sleep(-1)` or `time.sleep(1e20)` aborts the process instead of a catchable `Runtime` error — reject non-finite, negative, and overflowing values with `Error::Runtime` before constructing the `Duration`.
2. [BLOCKER] src/runtime.rs:488 — `time.format` does `UNIX_EPOCH + Duration::from_secs(timestamp as u64)` then `duration_since(...).unwrap()` — a large finite literal like `time.format(1e20)` saturates to `u64::MAX` and panics on `SystemTime` overflow, and a negative like `time.format(-1)` saturates to `0` and silently answers `1970` — validate the timestamp is a finite non-negative in-range integer and return `Error::Runtime` otherwise.
3. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:667 — `random_number`/`random_choice`/`random_shuffle` use `SystemTime::now().duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH).unwrap()` and wall-clock nanos as an unseeded draw — a pre-epoch clock aborts, and every draw is nondeterministic with no seed — replace `unwrap()` with a `Runtime` error and route draws through a seeded RNG.
4. [MAJOR] src/runtime.rs:272 — `runtime::builtin` refuses only `args.len() > expected`, never too few — bare spellings rely on per-arm errors with different wording (`length` vs `text.length`) while `stdlib::call_module_function` at src/stdlib.rs:205 refuses `given != expected` — check `!=` in both places so bare and module spellings refuse identically.
5. [MAJOR] src/stdlib.rs:528 — `text.join` stringifies every element with `item.to_string()` — `text.join([1, yes, [1]], ",")` coerces instead of refusing, contradicting the strict refusal for `text.uppercase(1)` and `list.length(5)` — refuse non-text elements with a named `Runtime` error.
6. [MAJOR] README.md:142 — `math.random(min, max)` and `time.format(ts, format)` are documented as fixed-arity, but `math.random(5)` draws from zero and `time.format(0)` answers with the default format per src/runtime.rs:658 and src/runtime.rs:480 and pinned by tests — correct the signatures to the optional-arity the code implements.
7. [MAJOR] AGENTS.md:195 — `PI, E` plus `pow/sin/cos/tan/log/exp` and `contains/starts_with/replace` are still listed as callable, but none is answered (`say PI` is `Unknown variable`, `say pow(2,3)` is `Unknown function` per phases/phase-032/FINDINGS.md §2/§8) — remove the unimplemented names or gate them behind their owning phase.
